  "finalText": "Marcus, I've cancelled R3311 (AA660, SFO→Boston, 2026-08-05). You're getting the full $248.00 back as travel credit, not on your card.\n\n- **Why credit and not card:** Your fare is Basic Economy, which isn't refundable on its own. Your trip insurance does override that, but only if you cancel at least 14 days before departure. The refund policy shows today as 2026-07-28, which is 8 days before the flight. Inside that window, the insurance turns the fare into travel credit and no money goes back to your card.\n- **Fee:** The $50 cancellation service fee is waived because you're a Platinum member. The credit is the full $248.00.\n- **Ledger:** There is one entry, L1, for $248.00 as travel credit. I checked the ledger after settling and there are no other entries.\n\nThe policy tool's date (2026-07-28) differs from the date in my task context (2026-10-05). I followed the policy tool's date, and the flight still showed as scheduled. I did not touch any other bookings.",
